 "design": "R6 what one size band would need on the accuracy scale, where the noise is twice as loud.\n\nDesign fixed before running (2026-09-16, written 15:45 EDT). snap-r6-single-size asks how many runs a\nsingle band needs before its margin interval separates from one. The accuracy scale carries about twice\nthe item noise at 1.45 against 0.73, and its true ratio on the full battery is 1.078 rather than 1.244,\nso the same sweep on accuracy is a much harder problem and the answer could be that no affordable run\ncount reaches it. That is a useful thing for the paper to be able to say, because it turns a vague\nstatement about weaker within-size evidence into a number a reader can act on.\nThis run sweeps the runs per configuration over 3, 6, 10, 16, 24 and 40 at a single band of 25\nconfigurations, on a population whose true ratio is 1.078 at the accuracy battery's noise, with 4,000\nreplicates each. It reports coverage, median width and the rate at which the interval excludes one. Seed\n20260971 keeps the draws distinct.\n",
